  "9ca87d0d00": "Niagara Falls",
  "3947ef9ead": "Amazon River Delta",
  "68a4ebb707": "Names of Large Rivers",
  "a9cfacdcea": "The native names of rivers often vary depending on the various enthnographic domains they pass through. In some instances, I have chosen the dominant ethonymn (e.g., *dijla* for the Tigris), in other instances I have combined names (e.g., *caňpobrahmaputra* for the Brahmaputra), while in others I have used a form derived from an underlying proto-language (e.g., *purát* for the Euphrates, *danu* for the Danube). The following names are preceded by *hluséi-welza* OR *welza hle’i / hi* ‘river named...’ (Carrier Stem 3 incorporated into Stem 2 of the root -**LZ**-).",
